Human factors and safety engineering (@human-factors-and-safety-engineering: 0, is #chapter, #outline) { r_20YMRH70QKZP2DBCSG4QX28B0J
This field studies interactions among people, tasks, equipment, organisations, and operating conditions. The material connects ergonomics, interface design, workload, error, hazards, system analysis, and learning from incidents, treating dependable operation as a property of the whole working arrangement.

**Common preparation developed:** the [people and operation review](../core/Review-operating-evidence-recovery-handover-and-discipline-entry.lingua) joins task context, operating-state evidence, error mechanisms, recovery and handover with the shared computing/inquiry formation. HSE/NASA passages support original paper scenarios and evaluation plans. No participant observation, human-error probability, physical protection or professional qualification is claimed; the full field remains pending.

**Parent:** [Engineering — systems, design, construction, and operation](../Engineering.lingua#r_5DA6VY09MAD2N8D9SH0FFJVV68).
} r_20YMRH70QKZP2DBCSG4QX28B0J
